WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:08.957
- [Mark] All right, Chanel.

00:00:08.957 --> 00:00:09.790
- Hi.

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:10.687
- [Mark] Chanel, where
are you from originally?

00:00:10.687 --> 00:00:11.620
Where did you grow up?

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.680
- [Chanel] I grew up here in LA.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.923
- [Mark] Here in LA.

00:00:14.923 --> 00:00:17.191
And did you grow up with
both parents, one parent?

00:00:17.191 --> 00:00:20.080
- [Chanel] I grew up with only one parent.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:20.913
- [Mark] Who was that?

00:00:20.913 --> 00:00:21.746
- [Chanel] My mom.

00:00:21.746 --> 00:00:24.893
- [Mark] Your mom? And
how was your childhood?

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:29.570
- I was kind of sheltered
and always told to step aside

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:32.170
and it will be done for me.

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:33.003
Until, you know,

00:00:33.003 --> 00:00:36.500
I had to grow up,

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.022
and it got to the point where

00:00:40.022 --> 00:00:42.520
I started to hold grudges,

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:47.520
and, you know, play the blame game and

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.525
stuff like that. And I don't know.

00:00:50.525 --> 00:00:52.060
- [Mark] Did you have siblings?

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.143
- I have one, yes.

00:00:55.427 --> 00:00:58.040
- [Mark] And so what age
were you when you discovered

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:00.990
that you were more comfortable as a woman?

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:01.823
- I was 12.

00:01:01.823 --> 00:01:02.810
- [Mark] Twelve?

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:05.870
How did that go with your
friends in school, and

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:06.703
stuff like that.

00:01:06.703 --> 00:01:07.536
And your parents?

00:01:07.536 --> 00:01:11.940
- I hid it until I was put

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:15.330
out of my house at 16 years old.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:20.330
And then I came out and
I've been out ever since.

00:01:24.018 --> 00:01:24.851
And I'm 29 at the moment, I'm sorry.

00:01:27.291 --> 00:01:29.110
I'm stuttering.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:32.465
- [Mark] (indistinct)

00:01:32.465 --> 00:01:35.400
So you're living on the street now?

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.233
- Yeah.

00:01:36.233 --> 00:01:40.000
- [Mark] And how long have
you been out here doing that?

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.530
- I've been here for five years.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:47.530
Every time I try to get
inside I'm always turned down

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:52.070
because they do not take me serious,

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:53.593
I believe. I don't know.

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:59.650
- [Mark] Do you find it's hard
being transgender in society?

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:02.130
Do you have problems getting a job

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:04.193
or getting a break from people?

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:09.420
- It's the stare into my
eyes that they give me

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:14.420
as if I'm a joke, or I'm, you know,

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:17.503
incompetent, I would say.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:22.193
But you know, it's always been something

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:28.790
that I hold onto my
conscious instead of talking

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:30.383
about it to people.

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:36.280
And I try to, you know, hide it

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:40.017
but it's starting to
hurt me more, and more,

00:02:40.017 --> 00:02:42.410
and more as I get older,
and older, and older.

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:43.243
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:02:43.243 --> 00:02:45.231
- And, yeah. So that's how that goes.

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.190
- [Mark] And stuttering kind of

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:47.530
complicates the issue, right?

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:49.160
- Yeah, it like-

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:51.393
- [Mark] So it's hard
enough being transgender,

00:02:51.393 --> 00:02:53.290
And then...

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:54.583
- Right, and I had a-

00:02:54.583 --> 00:02:55.830
- [Mark] (indistinct)

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:56.906
- Yeah.

00:02:56.906 --> 00:02:57.830
- [Mark] It's a struggle, yeah?

00:02:57.830 --> 00:02:59.735
- It kind of is, yeah.

00:02:59.735 --> 00:03:02.568
- [Mark] What do you do for money?

00:03:04.481 --> 00:03:06.802
What a lot of girls do on the street?

00:03:06.802 --> 00:03:11.740
- That does not work
for me anymore because

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:14.143
I find it to where,

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:18.200
I am not attractive to people

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:23.500
after they get into it or they see

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:28.500
that I can't perform
as you know, expected.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:35.350
So it kind of hinders the
whole confidence that I have

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:37.890
towards doing that.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:40.010
- [Mark] Why can you not perform?

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:45.010
- Because I'm uncomfortable
in the whole act.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:47.614
- [Mark] Oh, is that right?

00:03:47.614 --> 00:03:52.614
- Right, but it's kind of
grown to be expected of me.

00:03:56.050 --> 00:04:01.015
So I show it, but I don't act out on it.

00:04:01.015 --> 00:04:02.240
- [Mark] Oh, okay.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:06.900
- I try to tell people, no, no, no.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:09.973
And they still, you know, persistently.

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:16.210
So I kind of engage into
it somewhat, but into it,

00:04:17.118 --> 00:04:22.118
I try to stop or get it over
with as soon as possible

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:28.013
to please the person and
also keep me at peace.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:31.533
You know what I mean?

00:04:31.533 --> 00:04:32.366
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:04:32.366 --> 00:04:36.498
Have you been beaten
up anything like that?

00:04:36.498 --> 00:04:41.498
- I've been stabbed here
in my neck right here.

00:04:42.885 --> 00:04:45.658
I was stabbed.

00:04:45.658 --> 00:04:50.658
Here in my leg I was
stabbed and that's about it,

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:53.660
over the years down here.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:56.670
- [Mark] And what's your drug out here?

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:57.503
- Crystal.

00:04:57.503 --> 00:04:58.371
- [Mark] Crystal?

00:04:58.371 --> 00:05:00.381
- And I'm trying to stop it.

00:05:00.381 --> 00:05:04.310
I'm trying to stop it
so bad, but then again,

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:08.640
every time I get up, it's in my face.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:09.473
So I do it.

00:05:09.473 --> 00:05:14.251
I tried to cut back on
doing it and I have,

00:05:14.251 --> 00:05:19.251
I have. But it's still there, you know?

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:23.110
So I can't get over here just yet.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:26.765
I'm trying to though. I'm trying to, yeah.

00:05:26.765 --> 00:05:29.499
- [Mark] And do you still
have contact with your family?

00:05:29.499 --> 00:05:31.470
- My mom is dead.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:33.530
- [Mark] Oh, really? I'm sorry.

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:37.240
- So no, I don't have contact
with my family anymore.

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:42.240
And everybody else, they kind of hated me.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:46.013
So no, I don't have contact with them.

00:05:46.013 --> 00:05:49.177
- [Mark] Do you have any friends?

00:05:49.177 --> 00:05:54.177
- All of them kind of
shown me that they do not

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:59.730
like me neither, but you know
I still try to be as peaceful

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:02.743
and calm and cordial as possible.

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:08.650
But I'm dealing with a lot
of hatred, a lot of it.

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:13.650
- [Chanel] And I get over it
and still continue to talk

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:16.560
to the same people and do the same things.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:19.668
And it's hurting me. It's hurting me.

00:06:19.668 --> 00:06:21.357
- [Mark] It's hard to go through life

00:06:21.357 --> 00:06:22.234
without family or friends.

00:06:22.234 --> 00:06:24.310
- [Chanel] I try. Huh?

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:25.820
- [Mark] It's hard to go
through life without family,

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:26.653
or friends.

00:06:26.653 --> 00:06:31.510
- [Chanel] Right. So I turn
all of the negative, blah, blah

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:38.713
blah, blah, blah, to positive talk.

00:06:40.547 --> 00:06:45.547
And I'm kind of being
fake because I hear all

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:50.980
of them talking to me, but
I ain't paying attention

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:53.020
to anything that they're saying, because

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:58.240
deep down inside I'd be
like, okay, this person

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:01.600
is the same person who did this.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:06.150
So I'm holding grudges
towards them just as I did

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:08.400
towards my mother.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:12.943
And I'm trying to free
all of it, but it's hard.

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:20.400
It's hard to keep that good faith.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:21.870
I don't steal.

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:26.836
I don't do any of that to
anybody, but I do kind of

00:07:26.836 --> 00:07:31.836
hold that grudge against people.

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:40.170
I don't know how to take the steps towards

00:07:41.804 --> 00:07:46.630
gaining a good confidence,
strong confidence and

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:52.140
a good life in my future, I hope I can,

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:53.513
but I'm not...

00:07:53.513 --> 00:07:55.400
- [Mark] Do you have any
plans for your future?

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:59.986
- I was planning on
going to Paris to do an

00:07:59.986 --> 00:08:04.986
internship there but I would
have to stop doing drugs first

00:08:08.333 --> 00:08:13.253
and go into a full type of recovery.

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:18.052
- [Mark] Internship with what?

00:08:18.052 --> 00:08:21.990
- Journalism in fashion.

00:08:23.397 --> 00:08:24.230
- [Mark] Good for you.

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:25.545
- [Chanel] Yeah.

00:08:25.545 --> 00:08:26.820
- [Mark] That could be a nice change.

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:28.230
- [Chanel] That's what I wanted to do.

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:30.606
- [Mark] And getting off meth
would be a good change too.

00:08:30.606 --> 00:08:33.612
- [Chanel] Yeah, it would
and I'm trying my best.

00:08:33.612 --> 00:08:34.736
I'm trying my best.

00:08:34.736 --> 00:08:36.224
- [Mark] All right.

00:08:36.224 --> 00:08:37.945
Chanel, thank you so
much for talking to me.

00:08:37.945 --> 00:08:38.778
- Thank you.

00:08:38.778 --> 00:08:40.564
- [Mark] And good luck with everything.

00:08:40.564 --> 00:08:44.064
- I thank you so much, I hope so too. Bye.

